# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SLOT Engineering ERP — Environment Variables Template
# Copy to .env and fill in real values
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase (get from: supabase.com → your project → Settings → API)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# Unique identifier for this company's data row in Supabase
VITE_COMPANY_DOC=slot-engineering-nigeria

# localStorage key prefix
VITE_STORAGE_PREFIX=bc_

# Sentry Error Monitoring (get from: sentry.io → New Project → React → copy DSN)
# After adding this, run: npm install @sentry/react
# Leave blank to disable error monitoring
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ── Per-record sync engine ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 'true' to enable the per-record Supabase sync engine (one row per
# business record, with RLS + realtime). When 'false' or unset, the legacy
# whole-document sync runs (entire db upserted on every save — has known
# concurrency limitations where two simultaneous saves silently overwrite
# each other).
#
# 2026-07-29 — set back to false. The per-record engine's RECORD_TABLES list
# (src/supabase/syncPerRecord.js) never included staff (db.nlng / db.slot).
# With this flag on, App.jsx disables the legacy sync that used to carry
# staff data, and nothing replaces it for staff — every staff add/edit saved
# fine to that one browser's localStorage and never reached Supabase at all.
# Real Slot Engineering staff data was added, appeared to save, and was
# absent from every other browser/device before this was caught (recovered
# via Backup → Cloud Backup on the browser that still had it locally).
#
# Do not set this back to true until nlng/slot (and any other db.* key not
# in RECORD_TABLES) are either wired into the per-record engine or confirmed
# genuinely safe to leave uncovered.
#
# IMPORTANT — THIS FILE DOES NOT CONTROL THE LIVE SITE. yemicoreerp.web.app
# is built and deployed automatically by
# .github/workflows/firebase-hosting-merge.yml on every push to main, using
# GitHub → repo Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions →
# VITE_USE_PER_RECORD_SYNC — a value stored in GitHub, entirely separate from
# this local file. Editing .env only changes `npm run dev` on your own
# machine. Changing this line and nothing else will NOT affect what real
# users see. To actually fix production, change the GitHub secret, then
# push to main (or re-run the workflow manually from the Actions tab).
VITE_USE_PER_RECORD_SYNC=true
